==Battleground==
*1 [[Professor A.]] spawns as the boss after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Bun Bun Black]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With Bun Buns mandating the use of meatshields and Professor A. in the back to kill them off, this stage may be a vicious one. As a second Bun Bun will spawn once one of the initial enemies are down, there is no point in rushing down Bun Bun Black. Instead, use [[Long Distance]] units or [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wavers]] to snipe Professor A.

Using the Long Distance of [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Red Riding Mina]], [[Adult Cat (Rare Cat)|Prisoner Cat]] and/or [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Major Leaguer Cat]], or the [[Wave Attack|wave]] abilities of [[Manic Macho Legs Cat]] or [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]], one can freeze the Bun Bun Black with [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] to safely chip the Professor A. down. Bun Bun Black's high knockback count will inevitably end up baiting your units into Professor A.'s range, so it is necessary to lure him to the front after each knockback.

Anti-Floating CC units help ensure that killing the later Teacher Bun Bun will be quick, easy, and safe.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]: So long as the Bun Bun Black is frozen, Roe can help greatly with stalling the Professor A.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: A spammable waver with great damage for higher crown difficulties. Their performance can be improved through the use of Research [[Cat Combo]]s.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]: Without a doubt the most reliable option for pacifying Bun Bun Black. However, note that the aforementioned Bun Bun Black will also be knocked back often, clearing any Bombercats on the field.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]]: On {{4c}} difficulty, where Roe is no longer an option, Green Shell serves as a solid alternative. If [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter Cat]] is owned, however, he may be preferable due to his greater spammability and resistance to Floating.
*[[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]]: Only available from the game's [[Anniversary/13th Year|13th Anniversary]], but is a great complement to Bombercat due to his higher range.

==Trivia==
*OS Graveyard's Japanese name, Tomb of Mrs. Dos, is a reference to MS-DOS (Microsoft Disc Operating System), the main operating system for personal computers throughout the 1980s.

